-- title:
--   Conditional distributionally robust functional $\mathcal R^\star_{|\mathcal G}$, display (2.6)
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F)$ be a measurable space, $\{\varpi_i\}_{i\in\mathcal I}$ a finite partition of $\Omega$ generating the sigma subalgebra $\mathcal G$, $\mathfrak M$ a set of probability measures on $(\Omega,\mathcal F)$ (the **ambiguity set**), and $Z:\Omega\to\mathbb R$ a variable. The **conditional distributionally robust functional** of $\mathfrak M$ is the $\mathcal G$-measurable variable $\mathcal R^\star_{|\mathcal G}(Z)$ whose value on the atom $\varpi_i$ is
--
--   $$
--   \mathcal R^\star_{|\mathcal G}(Z)(\varpi_i)=\sup_{Q\in\mathfrak M,\;Q(\varpi_i)\neq0}\ \frac{1}{Q(\varpi_i)}\int_{\varpi_i}Z(\omega)\,dQ(\omega),\qquad i\in\mathcal I .
--   $$
--
--   The quantity under the supremum is the conditional expectation $\mathbb E_{Q|\mathcal G}[Z](\varpi_i)$ of $Z$ given the atom $\varpi_i$; measures that give $\varpi_i$ probability zero, on which this conditional expectation is not determined, are excluded. For a singleton $\mathfrak M=\{P\}$ the functional is the conditional expectation $\mathbb E_{P|\mathcal G}[Z]$. It is the conditional counterpart of the distributionally robust functional $\mathcal R(Z)=\sup_{Q\in\mathfrak M}\mathbb E_Q[Z]$ obtained by conditioning every measure of the ambiguity set.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The $\mathcal G$-measurable variable is represented by its values on the atoms, a function $\mathcal I\to\overline{\mathbb R}$ (extended reals). The supremum is taken in $\overline{\mathbb R}$: it equals $-\infty$ when no $Q\in\mathfrak M$ charges $\varpi_i$ and $+\infty$ when the conditional expectations are unbounded above. The factor $1/Q(\varpi_i)$ is the real reciprocal of $Q(\varpi_i)$, and the integral is the Bochner integral of $Z$ over $\varpi_i$; theorems that use the functional assume $Z$ integrable.
-- source:
--   Shapiro & Pichler, Conditional Distributionally Robust Functionals, preprint (October 9, 2022), display (2.6), p.4

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CondDRO_FinitePartition

open MeasureTheory

namespace CondDRO

/-- **The conditional distributionally robust functional** R⋆|𝒢 of an ambiguity set 𝔐, for the
finite sigma algebra 𝒢 generated by a finite partition `ϖ` (Shapiro & Pichler, *Conditional
Distributionally Robust Functionals*, preprint (October 9, 2022), display (2.6), p.4):
for every atom index `i`,
`R⋆|𝒢(Z)(ϖᵢ) = sup_{Q ∈ 𝔐, Q(ϖᵢ) ≠ 0} (1/Q(ϖᵢ)) ∫_{ϖᵢ} Z(ω) dQ(ω)`.

**Formalization Note.** The 𝒢-measurable variable R⋆|𝒢(Z), constant on each atom, is represented
by its value on each atom, a function `I → EReal` (the paper's notation Z(ϖᵢ) of (2.3)). The
supremum is taken in `EReal`, so it is `⊥` over an empty index set and `⊤` over an unbounded one
(never a junk `0`). The filter `Q(ϖᵢ) ≠ 0` of (2.6) is part of the index set. `1/Q(ϖᵢ)` is
`(Q ϖᵢ).toReal⁻¹`, which is the real number 1/Q(ϖᵢ) for the probability measures the paper
considers. The integral is Mathlib's Bochner integral over the restriction `Q.restrict ϖᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def condDRF {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {I : Type*}
    (M : Set (Measure Ω)) (ϖ : FinitePartition Ω I) (Z : Ω → ℝ) : I → EReal :=
  fun i => ⨆ Q ∈ {Q : Measure Ω | Q ∈ M ∧ Q (ϖ.cell i) ≠ 0},
    (((Q (ϖ.cell i)).toReal⁻¹ * ∫ ω in ϖ.cell i, Z ω ∂Q : ℝ) : EReal)

end CondDRO


